      "url": "https://www.last.fm/music/George+Michael/Faith",
      "wiki_content": "\"Faith\" is the debut solo studio album by English singer George Michael, released on 30 October 1987 by Columbia Records in the United States and on 2 November 1987 by Epic Records in the United Kingdom. Michael wrote and produced all tracks on the album, except for \"Look at Your Hands\", which he co-wrote with David Austin. Musically, \"Faith\" is a pop album incorporating elements of R&B, funk, and soul, with lyrics addressing personal and introspective themes that drew attention to Michael's personal life at the time.\n\nThe album reached number one on both the UK Albums Chart and the US Billboard 200. It remained in the top 10 of the Billboard 200 for 51 non-consecutive weeks, including 12 weeks at number one. \"Faith\" also became the first album by a white solo artist to reach number one on the Billboard Top Black Albums chart. Four singles from the album—\"Faith\", \"Father Figure\", \"One More Try\", and \"Monkey\"—topped the Billboard Hot 100, making Michael the only British male solo artist to achieve four number one hits from a single album on that chart. To support the album, Michael embarked on the Faith Tour beginning in February 1988, performing in Tokyo, Australia, Europe, and North America.\n\n\"Faith\" has sold over 25 million copies worldwide and was certified Diamond by the Recording Industry Association of America in 1996. The album received critical and commercial acclaim, winning Album of the Year at the 31st Grammy Awards. Michael earned three American Music Awards in 1989, including Favorite Pop/Rock Male Artist, Favorite Soul/R&B Male Artist, and Favorite Soul/R&B Album, and received the MTV Video Vanguard Award. The album is frequently cited as one of the defining albums of the 1980s and was ranked number 151 on Rolling Stone's list of the 500 Greatest Albums of All Time in 2020. <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/George+Michael/Faith\">Read more on Last.fm</a>. User-contributed text is available under the Creative Commons By-SA License; additional terms may apply.",
      "wiki_summary": "\"Faith\" is the debut solo studio album by English singer George Michael, released on 30 October 1987 by Columbia Records in the United States and on 2 November 1987 by Epic Records in the United Kingdom. Michael wrote and produced all tracks on the album, except for \"Look at Your Hands\", which he co-wrote with David Austin. Musically, \"Faith\" is a pop album incorporating elements of R&B, funk, and soul, with lyrics addressing personal and introspective themes that drew attention to Michael's personal life at the time. The album reached number one on both the UK Albums Chart and the <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/George+Michael/Faith\">Read more on Last.fm</a>."
